  "nl_text": "The database schema named \"schemabench_0221\" consists of five tables: Customer_Ratings, Customer_Details, Customer_Preference, Restaurants, and restaurant_cuisines.\nThe Customer_Ratings table holds information about customer ratings for various restaurants. It includes columns for Consumer_ID, Restaurant_ID, Overall_Rating, Food_Rating, and Service_Rating.\nThe Customer_Details table contains detailed information about the customers. It includes columns for Consumer_ID, City, State, Country, Latitude, Longitude, Smoker, Drink_Level, Transportation_Method, Marital_Status, Children, Age, Occupation, Budget.\nThe Customer_Preference table contains preferences of the customers. It includes columns for Consumer_ID and Preferred_Cuisine.\nThe Restaurants table holds information about various restaurants. It includes columns for Restaurant_ID, Name, City, State, Country, Zip_Code, Latitude, Longitude, Alcohol_Service, Smoking_Allowed, Price, Franchise, Area, and Parking.\nFinally, the restaurant_cuisines table contains information about the cuisines offered by the restaurants. It includes columns for Restaurant_ID and Cuisine.\nAll tables allow null values except for the Consumer_ID, Restaurant_ID, and Name columns in the Restaurants table. The default value for Smoker, Drink_Level, Transportation_Method, Marital_Status, Children, Occupation, Budget, Alcohol_Service, Smoking_Allowed, Price, Franchise, Area, and Parking is NULL. The primary keys are Consumer_ID and Restaurant_ID, respectively, in the Customer_Ratings and Restaurants tables. The unique constraints are on the Consumer_ID and Restaurant_ID columns in the Customer_Ratings and Restaurants tables. The foreign keys are Consumer_ID in the Customer_Details, Customer_Preference, and Customer_Ratings tables referencing Consumer_ID in the Customer_Details table. The foreign keys are Restaurant_ID in the Customer_Ratings, restaurant_cuisines, and Restaurants tables referencing Restaurant_ID in the Restaurants table. The update and delete rules are set to CASCADE for the foreign keys.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThis project involves analyzing restaurant ratings data to gain insights into the performance of various dining establishments. The focus is on using SQL to extract, transform, and analyze the dataset, identifying factors that impact a restaurant's rating. The dataset includes information about consumers and restaurants, covering multiple variables such as location, cuisine, and price range.\n\n Objectives\n\n1. Extract and analyze data to understand factors influencing restaurant ratings.\n2. Perform sentiment analysis to identify well-reviewed restaurants.\n3. Provide strategic recommendations for restaurants to enhance performance.\n\n Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Restaurant Owners: Seek insights to improve their services and customer satisfaction.\n- Data Analysts: Perform the analysis and generate reports and recommendations.\n- Marketing Teams: Use insights to tailor promotional strategies based on customer preferences.\n\n Functional Descriptions\n\n1. Data Extraction & Transformation: Utilize SQL to handle extraction and transformation of data from multiple tables.\n2. Rating Analysis: Analyze ratings based on factors such as location, cuisine, and price.\n3. Sentiment Analysis: Conduct sentiment analysis to determine customer satisfaction levels.\n4. Report Generation: Produce comprehensive reports detailing insights and recommendations.\n\n Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Performance: Ensure the system efficiently processes large datasets to produce timely insights.\n- Scalability: Support the potential increase in data volume as more ratings and consumer information are added.\n- Data Security: Safeguard sensitive consumer and restaurant information, adhering to privacy standards.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_deepseek/0221.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0221\nCREATE TABLE `Customer_Ratings` (\n  `Consumer_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Restaurant_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Overall_Rating` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Food_Rating` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Service_Rating` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Consumer_ID`, `Restaurant_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `Customer_Ratings_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Consumer_ID`) REFERENCES `Customer_Details` (`Consumer_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `Customer_Ratings_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Restaurant_ID`) REFERENCES `Restaurants` (`Restaurant_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Customer_Details` (\n  `Consumer_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `City` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `State` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Country` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Latitude` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Longitude` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Smoker` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Drink_Level` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Transportation_Method` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Marital_Status` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Children` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Age` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Occupation` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Budget` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Consumer_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Customer_Preference` (\n  `Consumer_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Preferred_Cuisine` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Consumer_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `Customer_Preference_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Consumer_ID`) REFERENCES `Customer_Details` (`Consumer_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Restaurants` (\n  `Restaurant_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `City` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `State` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Country` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Zip_Code` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Latitude` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Longitude` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Alcohol_Service` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Smoking_Allowed` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Price` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Franchise` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Area` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Parking` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Restaurant_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `restaurant_cuisines` (\n  `Restaurant_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Cuisine` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Restaurant_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `restaurant_cuisines_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Restaurant_ID`) REFERENCES `Restaurants` (`Restaurant_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
